  "findings": [
    "All three actual model-keyboard styles show q, caret, Select all and Done clearly above actual keys. Done frames show dismissal and retained draft value.",
    "Largest native selection of full gemini-3.8-flash is visible across both lines, unlike the failed R41 word-only selection. All six field replacements pass exact full-value assertions.",
    "Largest preference label uses full width, selected API key is complete, and real thumb on/off is visible.",
    "Largest long preset endpoint and client exceed the keyboard viewport; selected endings partly overlap the transparent accessory region in these stills. Native full replacement is verified, but these stills alone do not establish caret-at-end or complete long-field scrolling. Add ordinary overlapping endpoint/client ending captures if needed before visual acceptance.",
    "Largest built-in description screenshot ends before the final now/photo row; capture the footer through ordinary scrolling for complete current visual coverage.",
    "All66 originals individually opened and hash matched. Normal/dark modes have complete native choices, client/model/endpoint values and usable selection controls. Google saved/draft sign-in distinction and request disclosure are legible in ordinary normal/dark viewports.",
    "Largest native connection-choice popup shows the Google OAuth label only partially at the bottom of its scrollable menu. Functional selection passes; do not claim the entire menu label is visible in that one still. Add its ending capture if required for full visual acceptance.",
    "Largest Google sign-in/footer frames stop before the complete configuration and disclosure paragraphs. Complete ordinary overlapping footer captures are still required; passing mode tests do not close this pixel gap."
  ],
  "acceptance": "scoped functional six-case compact pass; current full visual/critic/publication acceptance open"
}
